# Third-party Claude Code skills (mattpocock/skills) - installed as editable copies
.claude/skills/

# Accounts. Password hashes, session tokens and someone's list of jobs they
# applied to. These live in their own file, separate from the scraped job data,
# and that file is never a git object.
data/users.db
data/users.db-shm
data/users.db-wal

# The Google OAuth client secret, when Google sign-in is configured.
config/google-oauth.json

# The Anthropic API key, when "describe your search" is configured. A key in a
# git object is a key somebody else can spend.
config/anthropic.json

# The same key, and any other secret, when kept in a .env instead. Same reason:
# a key in a git object is a key somebody else can spend. .env.example is the
# committed copy and holds no values.
.env
.env.local

# The scraped jobs database. 4.5 GB on disk and it changes every sweep, so it
# is never a git object — GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB anyway.
# Rebuild it from scratch with: npm run refresh
data/jobs.db
data/jobs.db-shm
data/jobs.db-wal

# The compacted copy ./deploy/upload-db.sh makes on its way to Fly, and the
# gzip of it (~857 MB). Rebuilt from data/jobs.db on every deploy, so there is
# nothing here worth keeping — and the .gz is well over GitHub's 100 MB limit.
data/jobs-deploy.db
data/jobs-deploy.db.gz

# Runtime state written by the sweeps, not source. The two reports are
# regenerated by every daily run on the laptop; data/sync-report.md stays
# tracked because the GitHub Actions slug sync owns it and commits it.
data/sync-state.json
data/daily-history.jsonl
data/daily.log
data/repair-ashby.log
data/daily-report.md
data/derive-report.md
progress/state.json

# The launchd job and its wrapper script. `npm run schedule` writes them with
# this machine's absolute paths baked in, so they are generated output, not
# source — the generator is src/schedule.mjs.
automation/

# Node and macOS noise.
node_modules/
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*

# The marketing landing page. Kept on disk on purpose — the code is not being
# thrown away — but it is not part of what this repo publishes and the server
# refuses to serve it (see PRIVATE in src/server.mjs).
app/landing.html

# Personal notes: interview prep, and the running list of things to improve.
# Never part of what this repo publishes.
RESUME-NOTES.md
NOTICED.md

# The working agreement for Claude Code sessions in this repo — branch/PR flow,
# commit style, the test gate. It steers how the work gets done; it is not part
# of what the repo publishes.
CLAUDE.md
